2026-06-30 15:48:16,789 - openai._base_client - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'timeout': 300, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-f13b2a9a-5342-4a3b-9dce-c615e5f0ed5a', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You are an expert SDRF-Proteomics annotator for crosslinking mass spectrometry (XL-MS) datasets.\n\nExtract the following SDRF metadata terms from the provided publication text and/or PRIDE project description.\n\nTERMS TO EXTRACT:\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nterm: sex\nsdrf_column: characteristics[sex]\nontology: PATO:0000047\ndescription: Biological sex of the donor.\nallowed_values: male, female, intersex, hermaphrodite, anonymized, not available, not applicable\ninstructions: Use one of the fixed values above. Return "not available" if not stated.\n  Return "not applicable" if the sample is from a cell line or organism without defined sex.\n\nterm: age\nsdrf_column: characteristics[age]\nontology: EFO:0000246\ndescription: Age of the donor at sample collection.\npattern: {Number}{Unit} where Unit is Y (years), M (months), W (weeks), D (days).\n  Also allowed: "anonymized" if age is stated but anonymized.\ninstructions: Return null if not stated.\n\nterm: ancestry category\nsdrf_column: characteristics[ancestry category]\nontology: HANCESTRO\ndescription: Ancestry or ethnic background of the donor.\ninstructions: Use HANCESTRO terms if possible. Return null if not stated or not applicable.\n\nterm: biological replicate\nsdrf_column: characteristics[biological replicate]\nontology: MS:1001809\ndescription: Identifier for the biological replicate (integer or "pooled").\ninstructions: Return a description of the replication strategy from the paper\n  (e.g. "3 biological replicates", "2 independent experiments"). The actual\n  integer values are assigned per-file automatically; describe what you find in the text.\n\nterm: genotype\nsdrf_column: characteristics[genotype]\nontology: EFO:0000513\ndescription: Known genetic variant, mutation, or genotype of the subject.\ninstructions: Return null if not stated. Example: "wild type", "Δatg5", "ΔYme1".\n\nterm: pooled sample\nsdrf_column: characteristics[pooled sample]\nontology: NCIT:C165587\ndescription: Whether the sample is a pooled sample.\nallowed_values: not pooled, pooled, or pattern SN=sample1;SN=sample2\ninstructions: Return "not pooled" unless explicitly stated otherwise.\n\nterm: phosphate\nsdrf_column: characteristics[phosphate]\nontology: PRIDE:0000805\ndescription: Phosphate concentration (only relevant for environmental/water samples).\npattern: number + mg/L or umol/L\ninstructions: Return null unless this is a water/environmental sample with explicit\n  phosphate concentration stated.\n\nterm: temperature\nsdrf_column: characteristics[temperature]\nontology: PRIDE:0000703\ndescription: Temperature at the sampling location (environmental samples only).\npattern: number + °C\ninstructions: Return null unless this is an environmental/metaproteomics sample\n  with explicit temperature stated. Do NOT confuse with crosslinking temperature.\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nReturn a single JSON object where each key is the exact sdrf_column string shown above.\nFor each key, return a dict with:\n  "value": the extracted value (string, list, or null)\n  "accession": ontology accession if resolvable, else null\n  "confidence": "high", "medium", or "low"\n  "evidence_quote": short verbatim quote from the text, or null\n  "evidence_location": location in the paper (e.g. "Methods"), or null'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '[TITLE]\nProteomic profiling of a healthy biological sample (human serum) obtained from the surface of the AFM chip.\n\n[ABSTRACT]\nMass spectrometric analysis was used to identify proteins from a biological plasma samples covalently immobilized on the surface of an AFM chip using cross-linkers SuccBB.\n\n[METHODS]\nTrypsinolysis Protocol:  Preparation of Reaction Mixture: To initiate trypsinolysis, prepare a solution containing:  10 µl of trypsin (concentration: 0.1 g/l) 50 µl of TEAB (50 mM) 1000 µl of deionized water Add this solution to tubes containing the AFM chips, ensuring that the solution completely covers the mica surface.  Incubation: Place the tubes with AFM chips in a shaker-incubator and incubate for 18 hours at 37°C, with agitation at 140 rpm.  Mixing: After incubation, transfer the tubes to a shaker for 60 minutes at 800 rpm and 40°C to ensure proper mixing.  Centrifugation: Subsequently, mix the tubes on a Vortex for 1 minute, then centrifuge for 10 minutes at 9000 rpm.  Post-centrifugation Procedure: Using tweezers, remove the AFM chips from the tube containing the tryptic mixture. Wash each side of the chips with 40 µl of acetonitrile using a laboratory dispenser. Collect the wash into the test tube with the tryptic lysate. Add an additional 40 µl of acetonitrile to the inside of the tube lid and close the tube.  Centrifugation: Centrifuge the tubes again for 10 minutes at 9000 rpm.  Panoramic Mass Spectrometry: For panoramic mass spectrometry analysis, use the Q Exactive™ HF Hybrid Quadrupole-Orbitrap™ mass spectrometer (Thermo Fisher Scientific, Rockwell, IL, USA). This instrument is capable of performing panoramic protein searches and is widely used in routine proteomic analyses.  Peptide Separation: Peptides from each sample are separated using high-performance liquid chromatography (HPLC) with the Ultimate 3000 Nano LC System (Thermo Scientific, Rockwell, IL, USA). A 15 cm long, 75 µm id C18 column (Acclaim® PepMap™ RSLC, Thermo Fisher Scientific, Rockwell, IL, USA) is used for separation.  Peptides are eluted with a gradient of 5–35% buffer B (80% acetonitrile, 0.1% formic acid) over 115 minutes at a flow rate of 0.3 µl/min. The total run time includes:  90 minutes to reach 99% buffer B 10 minutes of washing with 99% buffer B 15 minutes of re-equilibration with buffer A (0.1% formic acid).\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17', 'store': True, 'temperature': 0.3}}
